  "nl_text": "The rschema_0494 database is designed to manage a content management system, where users can create and interact with articles, comments, and categories. The database consists of four main tables: 'user', 'article', 'category', and 'comment_reply'. The 'user' table stores information about each registered user, including their unique identifier 'user_id', username, password, nickname, gender, creation time, and biography. The 'article' table represents the content published by users, with attributes such as title, author's 'user_id', cover image link, summary, comment permission, status, content, and metrics like the number of likes, dislikes, and reads, along with the creation time. The 'category' table organizes articles into hierarchical categories, with each category having a unique 'id', parent category 'id', level, name, description, and icon link. The 'comment_reply' table stores replies to comments, with attributes such as the unique 'comment_id', replied comment 'id', article 'id', user 'id', content, and creation time. The relationships between these tables are enforced through foreign keys: the 'article' table references the 'user' table for the author, the 'comment_reply' table references the 'article', 'user', and 'comment_reply' tables for the article, user, and replied comment respectively, and the 'category' table references itself for the parent category. The database uses InnoDB as the storage engine and UTF-8mb3 character set, with primary keys and unique constraints to ensure data integrity, and cascade delete and update rules to maintain consistency when related data is deleted or updated.",
  "gold_question": "A content management system specification is as follows:\nThe system accommodates multiple users. User information includes User ID, Username, Password, Nickname, Gender, Creation Time, and Biography.      \nThe system contains multiple articles. Article information includes Article ID, Title, Author, Cover Image Link, Summary, Comment Permission, Status, Content, Number of Likes, Number of Dislikes, Number of Reads, and Creation Time.\nArticles can belong to multiple categories. Category information includes ID, Parent Category ID, Level, Name, Description, and Icon Link, supporting multi-level classification.\nUsers can comment on articles. Comment information includes Comment ID, Replied Comment ID, Article ID, User ID, Content, and Creation Time.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_llama31/0494.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0494\nCREATE TABLE `user` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `username` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `password` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `nickname` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `gender` char(1) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `creation_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `biography` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `article` (\n  `article_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `cover_image` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `summary` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `comment_permission` tinyint(1) NOT NULL DEFAULT '1',\n  `status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `content` text NOT NULL,\n  `likes` int(11) NOT NULL DEFAULT '0',\n  `dislikes` int(11) NOT NULL DEFAULT '0',\n  `reads` int(11) NOT NULL DEFAULT '0',\n  `creation_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`article_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `article_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `category` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `parent_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `level` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `icon_link` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `category_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`parent_id`) REFERENCES `category` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `comment_reply` (\n  `comment_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `replied_comment_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `article_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `content` text NOT NULL,\n  `creation_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`comment_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `comment_reply_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`replied_comment_id`) REFERENCES `comment_reply` (`comment_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `comment_reply_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`article_id`) REFERENCES `article` (`article_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `comment_reply_ibfk_3` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
